verses.text:
“You are worthy, our Lord and God,
to take the glory, the honor and the power,
because you made all things;
it was through your will that they existed and were made.”{f}

That is why they stand before God’s throne
and worship him in his temple by day and by night,
and he who sits on the throne will spread his tent over them.{h}

Never again will they be hungry, never again thirsty;
no sun will beat down on them,
no burning heat,{i}

for the Lamb who is at the throne’s center will be their shepherd;
he will guide them to fountains of life-giving water,
and every tear God will wipe from their eyes.”{j}

Then I heard a loud voice in heaven saying,
“Now have come the salvation and the power
and the kingdom of our God
and the authority of his Christ,
for the accuser of our brothers has been thrown down,
who accuses them day and night before our God.{f}

By the Lamb’s blood they have defeated him,
and by the word to which they bore witness;
so little did they love their lives that they faced death.

If anyone is bound for captivity,
into captivity he goes;
if anyone kills with the sword,
with the sword he must be killed.
Here the saints are called to endurance and faithfulness.{i}

And I heard the angel of the waters say,
“You are just, you who are and who were, the Holy One,
because you have judged these things;{c}

for they shed the blood of saints and prophets,
and you have given them blood to drink.
They deserve it!”

And I heard the altar saying,
“Yes, Lord God, the Almighty,
your judgments are true and righteous.”{d}

For all the nations have fallen
through the wine of her passionate immorality;
the kings of the earth were immoral with her,
and the merchants of the earth grew rich
from the power of her luxury.”{c}

Pay her back as she herself has paid,
and repay her double for her deeds;
in the cup she mixed, mix her a double draught.{f}

Give her pain and mourning
to match the glory she gave herself and her wanton luxury.
In her heart she boasts,
‘Enthroned as a queen I sit;
widow I am not,
and mourning I shall never know.’{g}

Heaven, be glad over her,
and you saints, apostles and prophets,
for God has given judgment for you against her!{r}

No more will the music of harp and song,
of pipe and trumpet,
be heard within you;
never again will any craftsman of any trade
be found within you;
never again will the grinding of the mill
be heard within you;{t}

never again will lamplight
gleam within you;
never again will the voices of groom and bride
be heard within you.
Your traders were the great ones of the earth,
and by your witchcraft every nation was led astray.{u}

After this I heard what sounded like the loud roar of a vast crowd in heaven, crying,
“Hallelujah!
Salvation and glory and power belong to our God,{a}

for true and just are his judgments;
he has judged the great prostitute
who corrupted the earth with her immorality,
and he has avenged on her
the blood of his slaves.”{b}

And a second time they said,
“Hallelujah!
Her smoke rises to the ages of the ages.”{c}

Let us rejoice and exult,
and let us give the glory to him,
for the marriage of the Lamb has arrived,
and his bride has prepared herself.{g}
